A 2025 arXiv research paper by Tarik Anowar, Satyendra Kumar Mishra, Ripan Saha 1. Department of Mathematics, Raiganj University, Raiganj 733134, West Bengal, India2. Department of Mathematical Sciences, Indian Institute of Technology (BHU), Varanasi-221005, India3. Department of Mathematics, Raiganj University, Raiganj 733134, W. ABSTRACT

We develop a theory of
C_{p}
-Green functors of Lie type, unifying the axiomatic framework of Green functors with the structure of Lie algebras under the action of a cyclic group
C_{p}
of prime order.

A 2025 arXiv research paper by Yoshikazu Giga, Sho Katayama. We clarify existence and non-existence of graph-like forward self-similar solutions to the planar surface diffusion equations. Introduction

We consider the surface diffusion equation of the form

(1)

V=-\Delta_{\Gamma_{t}}H\quad\text{on}\quad\Gamma_{t}

for an evolving hypersurface
\Gamma_{t}
in
\mathbb{R}^{d}
;
here,
V
denotes the normal velocity of
\Gamma_{t}
in the direction of a unit normal vector field
\mathbf{n}
of
\Gamma_{t}
and
H
denotes the
(d-1)
times mean curvature of
\Gamma_{t}
in the direction of
\mathbf{n}
.
